#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "CAP-INGESTION Ingestion"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Files, in-place federation and change data capture behind one onboarding step."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-ONBOARDING]{1}, [CAP-CATALOG]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Data comes into the platform by the cheapest method that works, and none of it is lost or duplicated on the way."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Federation avoids making a copy at all, and change capture is only worth its cost for some sources ([P16]{1}). Treating the landing area as a queue keeps the source of record safe and makes failures visible ([P8]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "A landing area, with an archive and a quarantine."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Federated (foreign) catalogs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Change data capture into bronze."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "An archive sweep copies each file, checks its size, and only then removes the original. It leaves alone anything it can't account for."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "CAP-INGESTION.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Three ingestion methods are offered behind one onboarding step: files to a landing area, federation in place, and change data capture. The method is a value in the tenant entry."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Each method has a tenant entry in use or a test entry that plans cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "CAP-INGESTION.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "A landing area is a queue, not a store: accepted inputs move to a content-addressed archive after verification, and refused inputs move to quarantine with a reason. Nothing is deleted without a verified archive copy.{1}*Example:* A scanned register lands, is processed, and moves to the archive under its content hash; a file that cannot be read moves to quarantine with the reason 'unreadable page 3'."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "After a run, landing holds only unprocessed files; every quarantined file has a reason sidecar."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "CAP-INGESTION.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Ingestion tolerates at-least-once delivery: a re-delivered input converges on the existing record by content hash or natural key."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "Deliver the same input twice; row counts do not change."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "CAP-INGESTION.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "A source is federated in place before it is copied; change data capture is used where a copy is worth its cost; a custom extract is the last resort."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-ingestion.md
msgid "The tenant entry records why the chosen method was chosen."
msgstr ""

